  "root_cause": {
    "text": "In virtio_net's start_xmit, when napi_tx is disabled (use_napi=false) and IFF_XMIT_DST_RELEASE is cleared, the driver does not drop the skb's dst reference before enqueuing the packet, allowing a pending skb to retain a reference to a dst_entry whose dst_ops may be freed when its network namespace is destroyed, causing use-after-free upon later dst_release() during cleanup.",
    "evidence": "The commit message states: \"fix it by adds skb_dst_drop(skb) in start_xmit to explicitly release the dst reference before the skb is queued in virtio_net.\" The call trace shows dst_release being called from __free_old_xmit after the namespace has been deleted, accessing freed dst_ops. The patch adds `skb_dst_drop(skb)` in the `if (!use_napi)` block, confirming the missing drop.",
    "passed_review": true
  },
  "vuln_statements": [
    {
      "file": "drivers/net/virtio_net.c",
      "lineno": 3356,
      "content": "if (!use_napi) {",
